+      "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "PIN DELIBERATELY NOT ADVANCED - advancing it would assert a review that did not happen. STILL NEVER REVIEWED, and it is now the LARGEST single backlog of any fork: 64d528be7..ciru/main is 315 commits, 274 non-merge, of which 160 are 'fork-authored' by the --not upstream/master filter. That 160 is an UPPER BOUND, not a count: ciru shares NO ancestor with upstream llama.cpp (a re-import, not a fork), so the subtraction removes almost nothing. Author histogram as the sanity check: caf 55, ciru-ai 54, charlie12345 13, Ciru 8, Carlo Pasquale 5, Codex 5 - it does look mostly fork-side. Head moved to 112629f1e (2026-08-17, still moving daily); release/qwen3.8-activefpx-promptforge-v1 advanced to 152c42ff4 and two NEW tags appeared, qwen3.8-activefpx-promptforge-v2.1 and v2.2. Reviewing 160 re-imported commits is a lane of its own and is NAMED here rather than skipped quietly. WHAT THIS LANE DID ESTABLISH is the blocker that gates everything else - CONTRACT FLAG C: ciru MOVED type id 107. rocmfpx/main, the ORIGINATOR, has Q2_0_ROCMFPX=107 and COUNT=108, matching TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 3.1 verbatim. ciru/main has Q7_0_ROCMFPX=107 and Q2_0_ROCMFPX=108, COUNT=109, and BOTH ids are in ciru's gguf-py GGMLQuantizationType - ciru WRITES GGUFs tagged 107 meaning Q7_0. Severity is LOUD, not silent: block_rocmfp7 static_asserts to 240 bytes per macroblock against block_rocmfp2 at QS_ROCMFP2+2 = 10 bytes / 32 values, so row sizes are nowhere near each other. The damage is to the RULE, not to a file: contract section 3.1 says serialized ids are 'not ours to choose - we adopt whatever the format's originator serialized', and ciru and rocmfpx are now two originators disagreeing about 107/108. HQ CALL OWED before ciru is ever used as a port source. Full review: research/local-inference/2026-08-17-fork-delta-review.md",
