+      "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "THE OLD PIN WAS NOT MERELY BEHIND, IT WAS ON A LINEAGE THE FORK'S HEAD NEVER TOOK. c26cbdffc is 'Merge pull request #225 from TheTom/fix-ui-assets-partial-dist' (2026-07-18). `git branch -r --contains c26cbdffc` returns exactly two refs, turboquant/fix/vulkan-turbo3-flat-dequant-241 and turboquant/tom/merge-upstream-dsv4 - it is NOT contained by feature/turboquant-kv-cache, which is what origin/HEAD resolves to. merge-base(c26cbdffc, head) = 1fd6dfe9f, an UPSTREAM UI commit from 2026-06-14, and rev-list --left-right --count gives 338/841. So any 'c26cbdffc..head = 841 commits behind' figure is divergent-history arithmetic, not a delta. Re-pinned to f6124e914 (2026-08-17). The lane-110C claim above SURVIVES the move: the TurboQuant KV/WHT surface it measured is intact at the head, so this was a stale pin, not an evaporated finding. MEASURED DELTA from the merge-base: 816 non-merge, of which 151 are fork-authored (--not upstream/master) and 33 touch turbo/TQ quant or kernels; the other ~118 are upstream sync, DeepseekV4/DSpark, UI and CI. WHAT WE TAKE, ranked. (1) 7f8302613 'ggml-cpu : declare turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size extern, not a second definition' (2026-08-07) plus follow-up c7d6442dd (2026-08-12) - THIS IS A LIVE DEFECT IN OUR TREE. recut/2026-08-16 carries the pre-fix shape: ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:26 has `GGML_API int turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size;` inside extern C with no `extern`, and ops.cpp is C++, so that is a SECOND DEFINITION in libggml-cpu while the real one lives in ggml-turbo-quant.c:31-32 in libggml-base. The fix's own message names our platform: 'ELF interposition may merge them; two-level-namespace and DLL targets will not', so on our Windows DLL build the SET_ROWS handler and the quantizer plausibly operate on DIFFERENT variables and turbo3 group-size propagation is silently link-order dependent. CHECKED in source at both refs; NOT built or run - this lane's fence forbids builds, so the runtime consequence is reasoned, not observed. A build lane should confirm and take both. (2) cd4c3a1f6 'remove the per-call mallocs from the TurboQuant vec_dot kernels' (CPU, pure win). (3) e130aef60 'close complete-audit findings - 7 port regressions + TQ4_1S dp4a kernel' (an audit of exactly the port we did). (4) The Vulkan cluster of 2026-08-03/04, our backend: 844678bf2 SET_ROWS block decomposition for turbo weight types, 160649054 TQ MUL_MAT_ID size gate limited to the f16 dequant fallback, 5f5ef77ad TQ4_1S pipeline wiring, 4f2013d66 turbo3 KV pipeline, b43efe599 turbo3 wiring correction, 353ac109e + 637300387 mul_mat_vec_id add / MUL_MAT_ID reject, b514ae496 TQ3_1S weight type, b0c39adac TQ4_1S wiring restored - our merge 70a752991 post-dates these so several are probably already in, and EACH needs a content diff before cherry-picking (per-commit tree comparison across a rebase is a build lane's job, not a register lane's). (5) f050a2501 + a70a324fa fattn-vec turbo-K split for a VGPR spill, re-gated on the LUT rather than on D - authored for HIP/CUDA, but the gating correction is architecture-general. WHAT WE SKIP AND WHY: 3243b2875 (fused TQ3_1S mul_mat on HIP gfx1100 - our rig is a 780M gfx1103 on Vulkan, not HIP), 8365224ee (CUDA-only garbage-output fix), ffc210bfb (arm64 CI), 07e01ec54 + ce3dce77b + aab782c1b (DeepseekV4/DSpark model support - a different slot), and the ~118 upstream-sync commits which arrive with the next upstream move. CONTRACT CHECK: CLEAN. This head defines TQ3_1S=45 and TQ4_1S=46, exactly the ids TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 3.1 reserves, so verbatim adoption still holds. Runtime types sit at 43/44/47. FLAG E, the one silent-capable collision in the whole contract, CONFIRMED AT THIS HEAD: TURBO2_0 is id 43 and our Q2_0_G128 is id 43, and block_turbo2_0 (ggml_half + qs[128/4] = 34 B / 128 values) is BYTE-IDENTICAL AND FIELD-IDENTICAL to block_q2_0_g128, so gguf_init's row-size check has nothing to separate them and the g128 metadata gate keys off a marker a turbo2 file would never carry - a serialized TURBO2_0 read as our g128 would dequantize wrongly and KEEP GOING (turbo2 is WHT-rotated Lloyd-Max, ours is plain scaled). NOT TRIGGERED today, verified three ways at this head: no LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_TURBO2_0, no TURBO target in tools/quantize/quantize.cpp, no TURBO entry in gguf-py. Also, block_turbo2_0's in-source comment still reads '// 10 bytes total' while its static_assert computes 34 - contract section 1.1 warned about exactly those stale comments and it is still stale here. REGISTER DEFECT FLAGGED TO HQ, NOT FIXED HERE: this fork is registered TWICE - as this local_checkouts entry and as the `turboquant` git remote of the engine repo - and the two disagree. The sibling clone src/llama-cpp-turboquant is at a33ef00b1 (2026-06-23) with origin/feature/turboquant-kv-cache at fca3093c9, both OLDER than the remote head this pin now names. One of the two should be authoritative. Full review: research/local-inference/2026-08-17-fork-delta-review.md",
